sed for layout purposes, for instance, when we enable static tables. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anchor tag "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an HTML markup that generally contains a uniform source identifier or URI "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are header tags, anchor tags, and input elements server-side controls too?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "header tag "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a representation of a container to introduce navigation links and it typically contains different heading elements, a logo or icon and authorship information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are header tags, anchor tags, and input elements server-side controls too?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "runat attribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a source code that makes part of the declaration code syntax, it is mainly used in server- side processing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You normally have to write the HTML syntax of the element, but a runat=\"server\" attribute is also needed. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Phrasal verbs</span> are two part verbs; they generally consist of a verb and a particle which could be a preposition an adverb or both. Such particle assigns a new meaning or a figurative meaning to the verb it proceeds."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the following chart,  you will find some useful phrasal verbs  to express ideas related to web apps development: <br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":14,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Phrasal Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning/Common usage</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>account for</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to give reasons for to make or provide a reckoning of expenditure, payments to be responsible for destroying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>add up</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to find the sum (of), to result in a correct total ,to make sense, that is followed by to: to amount to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>deal with</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to take action on, to do business with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>end up</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to finish \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>pop up</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to appear, to happen \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>scroll up / down</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(on a computer display) to move a cursor smoothly, causing new data to replace old on the monitor\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>click on</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to press generally with a mouse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>hook up</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"with a computer and cables hook them up \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>turn on</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to start a computer \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>log in</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to access \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>wipe out</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to delete completely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>back up</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to duplicate, to support or assist\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>hack into </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to break into a computer system\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have a test tomorrow about HTML server controls.  But I don't have any idea of how exactly dealing with them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "HTML server controls are based on the standard HTML controls but they account for server-side processing."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "HTML Server Controls"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "HTML server controls are used to enable server side processing, which is a procedure to send information to a server in order to be processed. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a nutshell, <span class=\"strong\">HTML controls</span> are available for server- side processing once those become server controls by adding the<span class=\"italic\"> runat=\"server\"</span> and <span class=\"italic\">id attributes</span>. <br><br> There are different tags used for <span class=\"strong\">HTML server </span>controls: <br><br>  \uf0fc\tHeader tags: a header for an article<br> \uf0fc\tAnchor tags: allows you to programmatically access to the HTML tag on the server. <br><br>  The following table describes the HTML server controls: <br>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob08img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>Hi, I need you to give me some basic information about HTML server controls. How do you deal with HTML server controls?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Programmer: </span>Well, when you add a runat=\"server\" attribute to an HTML element.  Then, it can be treated as a server control. Those HTML server controls work within tags.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>What are the advantages of using HTML server controls in an ASP.NET framework? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Programmer: </span>HTML server controls help to get the information popped up in a web app. Thus, when an HTML element is not closed, ASP.NET does not recognize it, and the web page can mess up.  Also, HTML server controls are useful for layout purposes. However, are HTML server controls extremely necessary in compilation process? <br>"}, {"time": "60000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>Well, the ASP. NET framework does not require a well-structured HTML content, but a content with properly closed tags to compile. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Programmer: </span> I just figured out the way it works; the input elements need to have either anchor or header tags properly closed in order to run the information on the web. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>Exactly! In that way, HTML server controls are considered a great advantage to create static tables for the web content layout, and you can turn an HTML page into an available source to run on ASP.NET as well. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Programmer: </span>I see now. <br>"}, {"time": "100000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>Check out the programming language in this web page; scroll down for more information and tell me: What can you observe on that? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Programmer: </span>I noticed that the standard HTML tags are generally used for the page layout. Additionally, I see the ID attribute and the runat attribute are needed for the server-side processing to display data.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Martin: </span>Now, log in and back up the data on your computer. You're ready to pass. <br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n6le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le01ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give basic information about the HTML server controls in ASP.NET."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can mention ideas about the advantages of using HTML server controls in ASP.NET. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss some observations to use HTML server controls in ASP.NET."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think ASP.NET builds up modern web apps?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you figure out the role of HTML server controls in the development of web apps?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Getting to Know HTML Server Controls in ASP.NET "}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [3], "te